{"understanding":"The selected responsibility is applicable to enabled snapshotting after FSM application. Supplied code shows snapshot capture, sink finalization, file-backed publication with CRC and fsync, ordered listing, compaction, lagging-peer installation, and FSM restore. However, restart reconstruction and concrete LogStore behavior remain insufficiently evidenced, so recoverability after crashes or compaction cannot yet be established.","requests":[],"responsibilities":[],"patch":{"claims":[],"bindings":[],"relations":[],"units":[{"audit_question":{"disposition":"needs_specific_evidence","preferred_check":"source_review","requests":[{"file":"raft.go","start_line":361,"end_line":964,"reason":"Inspect startup, durable-state loading, snapshot discovery, and log/FSM reconstruction after restart."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1206,"end_line":1243,"reason":"Inspect the boundary between configuration processing and snapshot or recovery state publication."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1956,"end_line":1975,"reason":"Inspect adjacent recovery or persistence control code omitted from the supplied ranges."},{"file":"file_snapshot_test.go","start_line":1,"end_line":346,"reason":"Check executable expectations for FileSnapshotSink.Close, publication, listing, reaping, CRC verification, and failure paths."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot_test.go","start_line":1,"end_line":190,"reason":"Determine whether InmemSnapshotStore is test-only and whether its semantics are treated as an applicable variant."}],"question":"After a successful Raft.takeSnapshot and compactLogs call, can a legal crash/restart or lagging-peer recovery path always reconstruct the FSM state represented by the snapshot and continue replication? The discriminator is the missing startup reconstruction and concrete LogStore behavior: identify which durable snapshot metadata and bytes are selected, whether compacted indexes are recoverable, and whether recovery handles partial publication or deletion. The supplied file store uses temporary directories, CRC verification, file and directory syncing, and retention, but does not by itself establish crash-atomic metadata/state publication.","importance":"Failure would invalidate the meaningful guarantee that snapshotting safely permits log reclamation while preserving recoverable replicated state and continued replication.","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","file_snapshot.go:1:551","replication.go:137:387","fsm.go:16:285","README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100","log.go:1:192"],"participants":["Raft snapshot thread","FSM","SnapshotStore","LogStore","restarting Raft peer","lagging follower"],"objects":["FSM snapshot","snapshot metadata","snapshot state bytes","compacted log range","replication progress"],"contexts":["snapshotting enabled","FSM has applied entries","successful sink close","post-compaction restart","lagging follower installation","file-backed store","in-memory test store"],"event_paths":["Raft.runFSM captures lastIndex and lastTerm, then Raft.takeSnapshot obtains committed configuration and calls FSMSnapshot.Persist.","FileSnapshotSink.finalize flushes and syncs state bytes; FileSnapshotSink.Close writes metadata, renames the temporary directory, syncs the parent directory, and reaps older snapshots.","Raft.takeSnapshot publishes last-snapshot state before invoking compactLogs, which calls LogStore.DeleteRange.","Raft.sendLatestSnapshot lists snapshots, opens the first result, and installs it on a lagging follower.","Raft.installSnapshot stores, closes, restores, updates lastApplied and snapshot state, then compacts or removes old logs."],"points":[{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP1","phase":"establish","source_ids":["fsm.go:16:285","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"What exact FSM state and applied index does Snapshot establish before persistence, including concurrent Apply effects?","unknowns":["Concrete FSM implementation and snapshot consistency are not supplied."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP2","phase":"maintain","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:551","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B3"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Does successful sink publication make metadata and bytes jointly discoverable and durable before LogStore.DeleteRange can remove required history?","unknowns":["Crash behavior between metadata/state publication steps is not supplied by the interface."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP3","phase":"use","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B2","B3","B4"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Does List return the newest usable snapshot and does Open provide the same state after compaction?","unknowns":["Concrete LogStore retention and alternative recovery paths are unread."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP4","phase":"recover","source_ids":["raft.go:965:1205","raft.go:1244:1955"],"binding_ids":["B3","B4"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"question":"After restart or InstallSnapshot, which snapshot and log indexes are restored, and can subsequent replication proceed without missing required entries?","unknowns":["Startup recovery and durable-state reconstruction ranges are missing."]}],"trigger_rationale":"Use source review first to read the exact startup/recovery and test ranges, then compare the recovered snapshot-selection and log-retention behavior with the O1 recoverability relation. A direct test should be deferred until the legal prehistory, configured store variant, and restart reconstruction are established."},"code_uses":[{"binding_id":"B1","role":"direct","claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"relation_ids":[],"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"The unit checks the snapshot creation, persistence, publication, and compaction sequence." ,"unverified":[]},{"binding_id":"B2","role":"direct","claim_ids":["O1"],"relation_ids":[],"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"The unit checks the deletion boundary applied after snapshot creation.","unverified":["Concrete DeleteRange behavior remains unread."]},{"binding_id":"B3","role":"direct","claim_ids":["O1"],"relation_ids":[],"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","file_snapshot.go:1:551"],"rationale":"The unit checks the SnapshotStore contract and file-backed publication, listing, and reopening behavior.","unverified":["Crash atomicity and configured-store applicability remain unresolved."]},{"binding_id":"B4","role":"direct","claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"relation_ids":[],"source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"rationale":"The unit checks the consumer path that selects and opens a snapshot for a lagging follower.","unverified":["Follower restart and installation aftermath remain partially unresolved."]}],"coverage_intent":[{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP1","phase":"establish","source_ids":["fsm.go:16:285","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Recover the snapshot establishment index and FSM-state boundary.","unknowns":["FSM implementation-specific consistency."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP2","phase":"maintain","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:551","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B3"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Trace publication durability before compaction.","unknowns":["Crash ordering and concrete LogStore behavior."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP3","phase":"use","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"binding_ids":["B3","B4"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Trace snapshot selection and reopening for a lagging follower.","unknowns":["Configured store variant and restart behavior."]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP4","phase":"recover","source_ids":["raft.go:965:1205","raft.go:1244:1955"],"binding_ids":["B3","B4"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"question":"Trace restart and install recovery through continued replication.","unknowns":["Startup reconstruction ranges are unread."]}],"id":"U2","goal_ids":["G1"],"obligation_ids":["O1"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B3","B4"],"relation_ids": ["R1"],"scope":{"description":"Snapshot establishment through persistence, compaction, lagging-peer installation, and restart recovery for the configured SnapshotStore and LogStore.","assumptions":["The snapshot metadata index identifies the FSM state represented by the snapshot.","The documented SnapshotStore and LogStore interfaces apply to the configured implementations."],"excluded":["FSM implementation determinism beyond supplied interface text.","Unverified concrete storage crash guarantees.","Message fault behaviors not established by the supplied transport contract."],"parameters":[]},"rationale":"Bounded source-review unit for the persistence-to-compaction-to-recovery handoff. It preserves the existing goal and obligation while retaining the concrete store and restart gaps.","goal_observable":true}],"expected_versions":[],"rationale":"Add one bounded audit unit for the existing G1/O1 candidate relation. The unit remains evidence-seeking because startup reconstruction, concrete LogStore semantics, and executable store expectations are not fully supplied.","gaps":["Relation R1 is referenced by the existing unit draft but is not present in the supplied relation graph; dependency validation must resolve this before execution.","Concrete configured SnapshotStore and LogStore variants are not established.","Crash/restart behavior between snapshot publication, retention reaping, and log deletion remains unresolved."]},"exploration_requests":[{"reason":"Close the specific restart and concrete-store evidence gap before selecting a ready-for-check question.","responsibility_ids":["RESP1"],"requests":[{"file":"raft.go","start_line":361,"end_line":964,"reason":"Inspect startup, durable-state loading, snapshot discovery, and log/FSM reconstruction after restart."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1206,"end_line":1243,"reason":"Inspect the configuration and persistence boundary adjacent to snapshot recovery."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1956,"end_line":1975,"reason":"Inspect omitted recovery or persistence control code."},{"file":"file_snapshot_test.go","start_line":1,"end_line":346,"reason":"Review executable expectations for file snapshot publication, CRC validation, listing, retention, and failures."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot_test.go","start_line":1,"end_line":190,"reason":"Determine whether the in-memory store is test-only and whether its semantics are applicable."}]}],"limitations":["No semantic defect is confirmed: the supplied interfaces and file-store implementation do not establish complete crash atomicity or restart recovery.","The existing G1/O1 candidate meanings are preserved; this exploration does not revise them.","No execution or real-backend experiment is proposed until the missing source and configured variants are resolved."]}
